<%- include('../partials/head', { pageTitle, metaDescription, canonicalPath }) %>
<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Transparency</h1>
      <p class="lede mt-1">Every third-party service we use and do not use, how our search results are ranked, and our dark-pattern self-audit.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="two-col" style="align-items:start;">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Search and ranking</h2>
          <p>
            Product listings are ranked by our own merchandising order: pieces we are currently featuring first, then
            the rest of the catalogue. The sort control also offers newest, price low-to-high, price high-to-low and
            name A–Z, which are exactly what they say.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>We take no payment for placement.</strong> No seller can pay to rank higher because there are no
            third-party sellers on this site — we own and ship all inventory. If sponsored placements are ever
            introduced, they will be labelled “Sponsored” in the result itself, in line with the Consumer Protection
            (E-Commerce) (Amendment) Rules, 2026 effective 1 January 2027.
          </p>

          <h2>Pricing honesty</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>We do not display crossed-out “was” prices at present, because we are not currently running
              reductions. When we do, the comparison price will be the lowest price offered in the previous 30 days.</li>
            <li>No countdown timers. No “only 2 left!” unless the inventory figure is genuinely 2 or fewer, in which
              case it is stated as a plain stock count.</li>
            <li>No member-only price that appears after you enter an email. No fee that appears at the last step.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Reviews</h2>
          <p>
            Reviews are accepted only from signed-in customers with an order for that product. There is no import,
            seed or manual “add review” function, so fabricated reviews cannot enter the system. Products without
            reviews show an empty state that says so.
          </p>

          <h2>Dark-pattern self-audit</h2>
          <p>
            The Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) (Amendment) Rules, 2026 require a yearly dark-pattern self-audit and
            a displayed compliance certificate from 1 January 2027. We run the audit now rather than retrofitting it.
          </p>
          <% if (!audits.length) { %>
            <div class="empty-state">
              <p class="mb-0"><strong>No self-audit recorded yet on this deployment.</strong>
                The audit form is in the admin console. Until an audit has actually been recorded, this page will not
                claim one exists.</p>
            </div>
          <% } else { %>
            <ul>
              <% audits.forEach(function (a) { %>
                <li><strong><%= fmtDateTime(a.at) %></strong> — <%= a.detail %></li>
              <% }); %>
            </ul>
          <% } %>
          <p class="small muted">
            What the audit checks: false urgency, false scarcity, confirmshaming, pre-ticked paid add-ons, bundled
            consent, misleading button labels, hidden fees, difficult cancellation, hard-to-dismiss overlays, and
            asymmetric “accept” versus “reject” design.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="eyebrow">Third-party inventory</h2>
          <p class="small muted">Live from the same register that powers the cookie policy.</p>
          <table class="admin-table" style="background:#fff;">
            <caption class="sr-only">Third-party services and their status</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <% trackers.forEach(function (t) { %>
                <tr>
                  <td><%= t.name %><br><span class="small muted"><%= t.provider %></span></td>
                  <td><%= t.category %></td>
                  <td>
                    <% if (t.status === 'active') { %><span class="badge">active</span>
                    <% } else if (t.status === 'removed') { %><span class="badge badge--neutral">removed</span>
                    <% } else if (t.status === 'not_configured') { %><span class="badge badge--pend">not configured</span>
                    <% } else { %><span class="badge badge--neutral"><%= t.status %></span><% } %>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              <% }); %>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <h2 class="eyebrow mt-3">What the browser can verify</h2>
          <p class="small">
            Our Content-Security-Policy has no external origins in <code>script-src</code>, <code>style-src</code>,
            <code>font-src</code>, <code>img-src</code> or <code>connect-src</code>. You can confirm this in the
            developer tools network tab: the only external request this site can make is the payment gateway script,
            and only on the payment page after you choose to pay.
          </p>

          <h2 class="eyebrow mt-3">Disclosure of what is not finished</h2>
          <ul class="small">
            <li>Payment is running in <strong>simulator mode</strong> — no money moves.</li>
            <li>Email and SMS delivery are <strong>not connected</strong>; messages are logged for manual sending.</li>
            <li>No courier integration exists, so no live tracking numbers are shown.</li>
            <li>Product photography is illustrative, not photographs of the physical stock.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="small">
            Full detail and status per requirement:
            <a href="/launch-readiness">launch-readiness report</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
<%- include('../partials/consent-banner') %>
</body>
</html>
